-- The ground state. At every p in the bracket [a, b] of the root, A(p) lies in [A_lo(b), A_hi(a)] (A decreases as
-- p grows: G increases in A and decreases in p², through −p²/3 and s_2's numerator), and evaluating the radial
-- chain over those intervals encloses every r_n at the root. If every one is positive, every g_n is (the tail's
-- ratios lie in (0, 1]), so X has no node on ξ ≥ 1; A is the angular operator's lowest eigenvalue (G is increasing
-- on (−∞, 0] with G(−p²) < 0, so no root lies below), whose eigenfunction has no node; so ψ = X Y has none, and it
-- is the ground state.
h2p-ground : List Bool → List Bool → IV → Nat → Nat → Nat → IV → Bool
h2p-ground S S2 R M K N b = h2p-ground-at S S2 R N b
  (fst (ang-a S S2 (iv-mul S (snd b , snd b) (snd b , snd b)) M K (bz-neg (snd (iv-mul S (snd b , snd b) (snd b , snd b))) , bz-zero)) ,
   snd (ang-a S S2 (iv-mul S (fst b , fst b) (fst b , fst b)) M K (bz-neg (snd (iv-mul S (fst b , fst b) (fst b , fst b))) , bz-zero)))
